# Dependencies
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
# NOTE: Lockfiles (package-lock.json, yarn.lock) should be COMMITTED
# They ensure reproducible builds across environments

# Environment variables
# Environment files. Every .env* is a secret EXCEPT the committed *.example templates.
# Deliberately broad: .env.demo and .env.demo.rotation live in the working tree ON THE DEMO HOST
# and carry POSTGRES_PASSWORD, JWT_SECRET, INTERNAL_SECRET and DATABASE_URL, so an enumerated list
# leaks the moment someone adds a new name.
#
# NOTE: .gitignore does NOT support trailing inline comments. The previous
#   .env.*.users  # Simulated user credentials - never commit!
# was parsed as one literal pattern including the comment text, so it matched nothing and the
# simulated user credentials it named were never actually ignored. Keep comments on their own line.
.env*
!.env*.example

# Three non-template env files are already TRACKED and hold only public URLs and simulation knobs —
# no secrets. Without these negations the rule above matches them anyway: git keeps honouring the
# index, so nothing breaks today, but they could not be re-added after a `git rm --cached` without
# `-f`, and `git clean -x` would delete them. Keep the ignore rules agreeing with reality.
!apps/frontend/.env.production
!services/simulation-service/.env.production
!services/simulation-service/.env.test

